I'm wondering if omitting the submit button's name might cause issues. I also need to check if the disabled checkbox has the correct accessible name and label.\n\nIt seems I need to improve the auto-submission process to sync filters without stale navigation. I think using fetch could help with faster edits while preserving state. There might be some overkill in my current approach, but I want to make sure everything works seamlessly for the user."},{"type":"summary_text","text":"**Improving submission handling**\n\nI'm considering whether to fetch a new page or preserve submissions by capturing the latest fields. It seems that intercepting all forms and using fetch to replace them might cancel any pending submissions if they're filled in. I want the UI for filters to update instantly and reflect hidden rows synchronously. \n\nHowever, this approach adds complexity. Maybe an alternative would be to auto-submit via fetch and just transplant the relevant rows, allowing for immediate synchronization without losing input. This could prevent navigation issues while submitting searches or ranges."},{"type":"summary_text","text":"**Enhancing GET data submission**\n\nI'm thinking about creating a coherent approach for progressive enhancement with GET data auto-submit forms. I need to ensure that hidden fields with the same names across forms are appropriately modified while excluding visible ones. \n\nThe GET auto-select form controls should retain their state. When I fetch the response, I need to parse and replace the list while also considering the error handling and the container ID. I should abort any other submissions to keep things clean. Plus, I need to run browser tests to confirm that everything meets the expected source requirements."}]},"output_index":0,"sequence_number":312}

